   "html_text": "Turing's oracle can be seen simply as a mathematical tool, useful for exploring the mathematics of the uncomputable. The idea of an oracle allows the formulation of questions of relative rather than absolute computability. Thus Turing opened new fields of investigation in mathematical logic. However, there is also a possible interpretation in terms of human cognitive capacity. On this interpretation, the oracle is related to the ‘intuition’ involved in seeing the truth of a Gödel statement. M. H",
